  "description": "Rear garden: Holme oak (T1)- reduce branches over clients garden by 2.5m.&nbsp;Magnolia (T2)- reduce crown by up to 2m.Bay (T3)- reduce by 4mLilac (T4)- reduce by 1.5mCherry (T5)- cut down to 3mFalse acacia (T6)- reduce branches growing towards building back to previous cuts (2.5m off)Bird cherry (T7)- reduce by 1.5mReason: most of the work is aimed at getting clearance from the building and allowing more light into the building. The bay has ganoderma,with a four-year old fruiting body. Sounding with a nylon mallet reveals significant hollowing. The client is keen to retain the tree, but asignificant reduction is prescribed to reduce the risk of failure. The cherry that's being cut down to 3m is mostly dead, there are some livebranches low down - most likely a case of managed decline.",
